Name: Olin Cordell

This program implements a multiprocess word count function in C that counts lines, 
words, and characters in a file. The file is divided into chunks based on the number 
of child processes specified by the user, and each chunk is processed concurrently by a 
separate child. Each child opens the file, locates its assigned offset, counts the data, 
and sends the results to the parent via pipes. The parent reads the results from the 
pipes and combines them to compute the total counts.

To simulate and handle failures, child processes may randomly crash based on a specified crash rate. 
The parent monitors each child using waitpid(). If a child crashes or fails to return a complete result, 
the parent retries the job up to a max number of retries. If a job continues to fail 
after the max retries, the parent marks it complete and prints a warning that totals may be incomplete. 
This is done to ensure fault tolerance while preventing the parent from crashing.
